        "thinking": "I can add a `worker` condition to the `@paperclipai/db` package.json exports that points to an alternative entry point. Wrangler uses the `worker` or `browser` condition when bundling for Workers.\n\nAlternatively, I can add a subpath export for `@paperclipai/db/schema` that only exports the schema without embedded-postgres.\n\nBut wait - the issue is that many server route files import values FROM `@paperclipai/db` (not a subpath). They do `import { agents, issues, ... } from \"@paperclipai/db\"`. These imports go through the main `.` export which includes embedded-postgres exports.\n \nSo I'll create a worker-specific entry point that exports only the schema and Db type, then add a `worker` condition to the package.json exports map so Wrangler picks it up automatically when bundling. This keeps everything clean and non-breaking for Node and tests.\n\nNow for the `node:sqlite` issue — that's coming from `undici@7` being bundled, which is a dependency of `jsdom`. I fixed `assets.ts` to dynamically import jsdom, so it shouldn't be statically bundled anymore. But the error persists, which means either jsdom is still being pulled in somewhere else or there's another source I'm missing.\n\nLooking back at what I actually fixed — I only addressed the schema import path in `api.ts`, which doesn't solve the jsdom/undici problem. The server route files still import directly from `@paperclipai/db` and pull in the full package. The same two error categories are still showing up: `@embedded-postgres/*` and `node:sqlite`, so my last fix didn't address either of them. before (same 9 errors). So the assets.ts fix didn't help yet, OR the same 9 errors are both present still.\n\nLet me check: the embedded-postgres errors are 7 (different platform binaries), and node:sqlite is 2. Total 9. Before and after my fix it's still 9 errors. \n\nWait, but I only ran wrangler dev ONCE more after fixing assets.ts. And that run still showed 9 errors. But the assets.ts fix was committed... \n\nActually, I need to be more careful. The sequence was:\n1. First wrangler dev: 9 errors (embedded-postgres + node:sqlite)\n2. I changed api.ts dynamic imports to use schema path\n3. I changed assets.ts jsdom to be a dynamic import\n4. Second wrangler dev: STILL 9 errors\n\nSo the embedded-postgres issue is coming from server routes that statically import from `@paperclipai/db`, which means I need to add the worker export condition to that package's configuration to properly handle the bundling.\n\nThe real problem is that esbuild bundles dynamic imports by default if they can be resolved, so making jsdom a dynamic import in the function doesn't actually exclude it from the bundle. I need to explicitly mark jsdom as external or use a worker-specific export condition to prevent it from being bundled at all. I need to actually verify what Wrangler 3.114.17 supports for handling external dependencies rather than just assuming.",
